  "final_output": "## Root cause\nThe 08:42 UTC Delivery carrier profile cut the booking deadline from 5 seconds to 450 ms. The 450 ms deadline was below the normal carrier p95 of about 668 ms. The client cancelled calls at the deadline before a carrier HTTP response. Delivery persisted the failed attempts for retry.\n\n## Evidence\nCarrier telemetry shows elevated client errors around the page during 08:42 to 09:10 UTC. Trace 739bba8ae0dacf84237c55fa655d5891 shows the client deadline and the retry insert. The Delivery settings logs show 450 ms at 08:42 and 5000 ms at 09:10. The 01:00 maintenance logs show HTTP 503 responses. The 08:42 failure is a client cancellation with no HTTP response.\n\n## Customer impact\nPaid orders waited for shipment booking. Delivery recorded 548 queued booking retries. Order ord_N4VMCY shows successful payment and confirmation, a queued booking, and a later successful retry.\n\n## Next steps\nThe 09:10 UTC rollback restored the five-second setting, and the ThirdPartyErrors page cleared at 09:10. Delivery logged zero pending retries at 09:22 UTC. No immediate action is needed. Monitor booking errors and reconcile by order reference before replaying any future timed-out bookings, since a cancelled request may have reached the carrier."
}
